1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:02,233
This series was created
for entertainment purposes.

2
00:00:02,234 --> 00:00:05,666
The characters, actions, locations,
dialogue, languages, ceremonies,

3
00:00:05,667 --> 00:00:08,132
and artistic elements depicted in this series

4
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:10,032
are fictional and based on imagination,

5
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:13,933
incorporating the beauty
of the region's diverse cultures,

6
00:00:13,934 --> 00:00:18,399
including those
of Lanna, Myanmar, the Tai peoples, and China.

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,566
It is not intended to disrespect any history,

8
00:00:20,567 --> 00:00:23,601
ethnic group, organization, profession,
or group of individuals.

9
00:00:23,602 --> 00:00:26,039
Viewer discretion is advised.

10
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:28,440
[Previously]
<i>This is a grave matter, Mueang Fah.</i>

11
00:00:28,441 --> 00:00:30,733
<i>I believe you love Ullavee</i>

12
00:00:30,734 --> 00:00:33,199
<i>and you will not let someone
like Prince Pha Wiang</i>

13
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,800
<i>profit off our kingdom.</i>

14
00:00:34,801 --> 00:00:37,433
<i>What you've heard is false.</i>

15
00:00:37,434 --> 00:00:38,800
<i>But there were witnesses.</i>

16
00:00:38,801 --> 00:00:39,900
<i>Some people died.</i>

17
00:00:39,901 --> 00:00:40,999
<i>That wretched Mueang Fah.</i>

18
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,833
<i>He keeps finding ways
to cause me trouble at every turn.</i>

19
00:00:42,834 --> 00:00:48,433
<i>If you hadn't shown him a weakness to exploit,
you wouldn't have to be angry now.</i>

20
00:00:48,434 --> 00:00:50,066
<i>That's the fortune-teller uncle.</i>

21
00:00:50,067 --> 00:00:52,066
<i>Fortune teller!</i>

22
00:00:52,067 --> 00:00:53,334
<i>Uncle!</i>

23
00:01:00,501 --> 00:01:03,132
<i>For patients with leg pain,</i>

24
00:01:03,133 --> 00:01:05,767
<i>the problem often originates
in the piriformis muscle.</i>

25
00:01:08,267 --> 00:01:10,999
<i>Ma'am, may I?</i>

26
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,399
<i>Ms. Boon, could you help me
turn your mother over?</i>

27
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:15,266
<i>- Yes.
- Here we go.</i>

28
00:01:15,267 --> 00:01:16,968
<i>One, two, three.</i>

29
00:01:18,167 --> 00:01:19,167
<i>All right.</i>

30
00:01:22,601 --> 00:01:24,934
<i>The piriformis muscle is right here.</i>

31
00:01:26,133 --> 00:01:27,968
<i>This might hurt a little, ma'am.</i>

32
00:01:31,968 --> 00:01:34,500
<i>This is called piriformis syndrome.</i>

33
00:01:34,501 --> 00:01:36,763
<i>It happens
when the piriformis muscle compresses a nerve.</i>

34
00:01:36,764 --> 00:01:37,879
<i>It usually occurs</i>

35
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:39,637
<i>when someone stays in the same position
for too long,</i>

36
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:41,840
<i>whether sitting, standing, or lying down
for extended periods,</i>

37
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:43,280
<i>like your mother.</i>

38
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:52,199
<i>This causes the piriformis muscle to tighten</i>

39
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,566
<i>and put pressure on the sciatic nerve,
resulting in leg pain.</i>

40
00:01:54,567 --> 00:01:58,200
<i>Some people may also experience
numbness or muscle weakness.</i>

41
00:02:00,267 --> 00:02:02,767
<i>Let's have Na Boon help massage the muscle
to loosen it up, ma'am.</i>

42
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:07,567
<i>Right here.</i>

43
00:02:11,334 --> 00:02:13,100
<i>Form a triangle with your hands.</i>

44
00:02:15,601 --> 00:02:17,166
<i>May I?</i>

45
00:02:17,167 --> 00:02:19,934
<i>Link your thumbs together, then press down.</i>

46
00:02:20,767 --> 00:02:22,701
<i>Hold it for three seconds. That's right.</i>

47
00:02:23,534 --> 00:02:26,133
<i>It might sting a little, Mom,
but you'll feel better.</i>

48
00:02:36,667 --> 00:02:37,934
<i>Good.</i>

49
00:02:52,167 --> 00:02:54,167
<i>Thank you so much, Mr. Bew.</i>

50
00:02:56,767 --> 00:02:58,200
<i>My pleasure.</i>

51
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,239
<i>Don't forget to apply a warm compress
to the painful area</i>

52
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:07,560
<i>for your mom.</i>

53
00:03:07,567 --> 00:03:10,399
<i>10 to 20 minutes a day should be enough.</i>

54
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,800
<i>My mom should sleep much better tonight.</i>

55
00:03:12,801 --> 00:03:16,132
<i>Thank you so much
for teaching me the physical therapy exercises</i>

56
00:03:16,133 --> 00:03:19,067
<i>and even showing me
those foot massage techniques.</i>

57
00:03:20,133 --> 00:03:23,719
<i>If you forget any of the exercises,
just give me a call.</i>

58
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,999
<i>And if you'd like to learn more about nutrition
for your mom,</i>

59
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,600
<i>let me know.</i>

60
00:03:27,601 --> 00:03:29,666
<i>I have a friend who can help.</i>

61
00:03:29,667 --> 00:03:31,133
<i>Thank you.</i>

62
00:03:32,634 --> 00:03:35,766
<i>Our next session is on Saturday, right?</i>

63
00:03:35,767 --> 00:03:37,067
<i>That's right.</i>

64
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:52,199
<i>There's a glass door between us now,
so I think it's okay.</i>

65
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,967
<i>Could you take off your mask for a moment?</i>

66
00:03:53,968 --> 00:03:57,300
<i>In case we run into each other somewhere else,
I'd like to be able to recognize you.</i>

67
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,701
<i>Now we'll be able to recognize each other.</i>

68
00:04:23,067 --> 00:04:25,133
<i>Thank you for the drink.</i>

69
00:04:26,968 --> 00:04:28,767
<i>I hope you like it.</i>

70
00:04:30,734 --> 00:04:32,200
<i>Of course I do.</i>

71
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:50,280
[Star Dust]

72
00:07:29,868 --> 00:07:32,266
If I hadn't pulled you out of the way,

73
00:07:32,267 --> 00:07:34,334
that horse would've trampled you to death.

74
00:07:35,534 --> 00:07:39,133
Every time we cross paths,
you're always one step from dying.

75
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:43,079
I was just out for a walk.

76
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:44,080
Look who's talking.

77
00:07:44,081 --> 00:07:47,880
Every time you show up,
I nearly get myself killed.

78
00:07:49,934 --> 00:07:51,933
So now it's my fault?

79
00:07:51,934 --> 00:07:54,501
I never said it was anyone's fault.

80
00:07:57,133 --> 00:07:58,334
Never mind.

81
00:07:59,434 --> 00:08:01,067
Anyway...

82
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:06,567
Thank you for saving my life.

83
00:08:07,167 --> 00:08:11,399
And thank you...

84
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:13,834
for giving me a reason to live again.

85
00:08:19,834 --> 00:08:21,601
I've been thinking...

86
00:08:23,234 --> 00:08:25,400
about what you said the other day.

87
00:08:26,634 --> 00:08:29,199
You were right.

88
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:34,167
We're not born... just to die.

89
00:08:35,534 --> 00:08:37,666
So I've made up my mind.

90
00:08:37,667 --> 00:08:40,233
I'm going to make the most of my life.

91
00:08:40,234 --> 00:08:42,200
I'm going to have a blast!

92
00:09:03,467 --> 00:09:04,968
Hey! Wait!

93
00:09:16,033 --> 00:09:18,333
If we meet again,

94
00:09:18,334 --> 00:09:20,700
I hope you're still alive.

95
00:09:20,701 --> 00:09:23,233
Why would you say that, Your Highness?

96
00:09:23,234 --> 00:09:25,200
Of course I'll still be alive!

97
00:09:25,934 --> 00:09:28,266
I'm going to live a long, happy life.

98
00:09:28,267 --> 00:09:30,867
After all, I've been given a second chance
as a noblewoman.

99
00:09:30,868 --> 00:09:34,267
I'm going to live like a fabulous lady!

100
00:09:38,801 --> 00:09:40,868
You're as ridiculous as ever.

101
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:43,280
I'll see you

102
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:45,440
at Prince Kong Tai's
birthday celebration, Your Highness.

103
00:09:47,968 --> 00:09:49,534
You'll be there, won't you?

104
00:10:07,868 --> 00:10:09,234
Where am I now?

105
00:10:10,334 --> 00:10:11,567
How do I get back?

106
00:10:15,267 --> 00:10:16,300
But...

107
00:10:17,667 --> 00:10:19,733
I came from that way.

108
00:10:19,734 --> 00:10:22,400
So... I should just go back that way.

109
00:10:33,033 --> 00:10:34,801
<i>You've been through a lot.</i>

110
00:10:37,634 --> 00:10:41,566
<i>You lost your parents and the people you loved.</i>

111
00:10:41,567 --> 00:10:44,767
<i>Your boyfriend sucks. Your friend betrayed you.</i>

112
00:10:45,467 --> 00:10:46,567
<i>Am I right?</i>

113
00:10:48,467 --> 00:10:49,667
Eva.

114
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:52,467
The fortune teller.

115
00:11:01,467 --> 00:11:03,234
Lady Fongnuan.

116
00:11:04,434 --> 00:11:06,534
Why are you still awake?

117
00:11:09,467 --> 00:11:13,601
If you stay out in the night air for too long,
you'll fall ill.

118
00:11:14,267 --> 00:11:15,934
I can't stop thinking about it.

119
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:19,534
Eva...

120
00:11:22,467 --> 00:11:24,433
Lha...

121
00:11:24,434 --> 00:11:28,800
You said... we have 32 souls.

122
00:11:28,801 --> 00:11:31,200
Almost as if we have 32 lives.

123
00:11:35,667 --> 00:11:37,701
Does that mean...

124
00:11:39,033 --> 00:11:42,800
When we die, can we be reborn?

125
00:11:42,801 --> 00:11:46,033
Can we meet again in another life?

126
00:11:46,634 --> 00:11:49,334
Is that what's keeping you awake?

127
00:11:51,834 --> 00:11:54,700
As long as our souls stay with us,

128
00:11:54,701 --> 00:11:57,399
we remain healthy and well.

129
00:11:57,400 --> 00:12:01,500
But when they leave, we fall ill.

130
00:12:01,501 --> 00:12:07,400
We have to perform a ritual...
to call them back.

131
00:12:09,167 --> 00:12:13,766
If they don't return, we die.

132
00:12:13,767 --> 00:12:19,099
Then our 32 souls are reborn into 32 new lives.

133
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:24,266
Perhaps we've died and been reborn many times.

134
00:12:24,267 --> 00:12:27,033
Only to meet in this life, my lady.

135
00:12:42,267 --> 00:12:44,267
So, besides me...

136
00:12:46,467 --> 00:12:48,033
Eva...

137
00:12:49,033 --> 00:12:50,834
and the fortune teller,

138
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,567
who else will show up?

139
00:13:19,467 --> 00:13:21,267
Welcome, Your Highness.

140
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,567
Prince Mueang Fah.

141
00:13:32,167 --> 00:13:33,801
You're here too?

142
00:13:35,434 --> 00:13:36,734
Mueang Fah!

143
00:13:38,601 --> 00:13:40,766
You two know each other?

144
00:13:40,767 --> 00:13:42,766
When did you meet?

145
00:13:42,767 --> 00:13:45,466
How did you meet?

146
00:13:45,467 --> 00:13:48,800
That's a long story. Want to hear it?

147
00:13:48,801 --> 00:13:50,234
Don't you dare.

148
00:13:53,334 --> 00:13:55,199
Today is Kong Tai's birthday.

149
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,999
Let's not keep the celebrations waiting.

150
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,400
Let's raise our cups
and wish Kong Tai a happy birthday.

151
00:14:03,267 --> 00:14:04,733
But...

152
00:14:04,734 --> 00:14:07,868
The seer told me to keep the Five Precepts.

153
00:14:14,434 --> 00:14:16,733
But it's my birthday.

154
00:14:16,734 --> 00:14:19,434
Surely one little drink won't hurt.

155
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:25,701
Then let's drink to our hearts' content.
And no one leaves early.

156
00:14:29,801 --> 00:14:33,234
Have a wonderful time.
I've taken care of everything.

157
00:14:57,067 --> 00:15:01,800
This celebration is my birthday gift to you.

158
00:15:01,801 --> 00:15:06,533
Everyone here joins me
in raising a toast to you, Kong Tai.

159
00:15:06,534 --> 00:15:09,834
I'm afraid I haven't brought you a gift.

160
00:15:11,167 --> 00:15:13,767
You'll have to accept Saen Thep's gift
on my behalf.

161
00:15:15,834 --> 00:15:17,367
Thank you, Sister.

162
00:15:32,501 --> 00:15:34,233
And this...

163
00:15:34,234 --> 00:15:35,868
is my gift to you.

164
00:15:51,033 --> 00:15:53,133
What a beautiful dagger!

165
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,667
I love it!

166
00:15:59,033 --> 00:16:01,533
Kong Tai. Careful!

167
00:16:01,534 --> 00:16:02,868
Watch this.

168
00:16:05,033 --> 00:16:06,534
Kong Tai!

169
00:16:07,167 --> 00:16:08,634
Put that away.

170
00:16:13,534 --> 00:16:17,000
And here's... my gift to you.

171
00:16:20,033 --> 00:16:21,033
Fongnuan.

172
00:16:26,467 --> 00:16:31,466
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

173
00:16:31,467 --> 00:16:36,132
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

174
00:16:36,133 --> 00:16:37,199
<i>♪ Happy birth- ♪</i>

175
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,968
What on earth are you singing?

176
00:16:39,734 --> 00:16:41,534
I haven't the faintest idea what that means.

177
00:16:48,968 --> 00:16:51,167
I haven't even finished the song!

178
00:16:52,334 --> 00:16:54,501
How can you judge it already?

179
00:17:04,434 --> 00:17:08,633
Was that a birthday song...

180
00:17:08,634 --> 00:17:10,667
from Wang Nam Lin?

181
00:17:17,834 --> 00:17:19,567
Yes, Your Highness.

182
00:17:21,167 --> 00:17:23,166
Everyone in Wang Nam Lin...

183
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,400
knows that song.

184
00:17:28,601 --> 00:17:29,801
I see.

185
00:17:32,968 --> 00:17:37,399
That song is going to be a huge hit.
Everyone around the world will sing it.

186
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:39,634
Let's hear the rest of it!

187
00:17:40,734 --> 00:17:45,500
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

188
00:17:45,501 --> 00:17:50,132
<i>- ♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>
- Yoo. Yoo!

189
00:17:50,133 --> 00:17:55,199
<i>♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪</i>

190
00:17:55,200 --> 00:18:00,601
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

191
00:18:03,434 --> 00:18:08,100
Why doesn't everyone sing along?
The more, the merrier.

192
00:18:11,133 --> 00:18:15,066
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

193
00:18:15,067 --> 00:18:20,701
<i>- ♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>
- Yoo... Heavens!

194
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:24,633
You all carry on.

195
00:18:24,634 --> 00:18:26,300
My head hurts!

196
00:18:30,734 --> 00:18:32,501
My ears hurt.

197
00:18:50,601 --> 00:18:53,733
It was only the slow version.

198
00:18:53,734 --> 00:18:56,466
Now, let's try the more upbeat version.

199
00:18:56,467 --> 00:18:58,566
Dance! Prince Fah Haam.

200
00:18:58,567 --> 00:19:01,400
Dans? Dans?

201
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:09,839
All right!

202
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:11,633
Kong Tai,

203
00:19:11,634 --> 00:19:17,567
I offer this performance to you...
as a birthday gift.

204
00:19:23,267 --> 00:19:27,132
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

205
00:19:27,133 --> 00:19:30,399
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i> Come on!

206
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:35,901
<i>♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪</i>

207
00:19:36,968 --> 00:19:38,767
<i>♪ Happy birth... ♪</i>

208
00:19:39,601 --> 00:19:42,200
<i>♪ Happy birth... ♪</i>

209
00:19:45,133 --> 00:19:46,666
<i>♪ Day ♪</i>

210
00:19:46,667 --> 00:19:47,999
Just say it.

211
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,967
<i>♪ To you ♪</i>

212
00:19:49,968 --> 00:19:51,766
<i>- ♪ Yooo... ♪
- ♪ Yooo... ♪</i>

213
00:19:51,767 --> 00:19:52,901
Yoo!

214
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:55,834
Yoo.

215
00:19:56,634 --> 00:19:58,600
Prince Kong Tai.

216
00:19:58,601 --> 00:20:00,200
<i>♪ Happy birth... ♪</i>

217
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,566
Just follow my lead.

218
00:20:02,567 --> 00:20:05,399
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i> Come on!

219
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:10,800
<i>- ♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪</i>
- Day!

220
00:20:10,801 --> 00:20:14,433
<i>♪ Happy birthday to... ♪</i>

221
00:20:14,434 --> 00:20:16,801
- You!
- Yoo!

222
00:20:18,367 --> 00:20:20,967
- You!
- Yoo!

223
00:20:20,968 --> 00:20:22,366
That's right.

224
00:20:22,367 --> 00:20:25,066
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

225
00:20:25,067 --> 00:20:26,166
- You!
- Yoo!

226
00:20:26,167 --> 00:20:28,299
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

227
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:30,066
- You!
- Yoo!

228
00:20:30,067 --> 00:20:34,099
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

229
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:37,166
<i>♪ Happy birthday to... ♪</i>

230
00:20:37,167 --> 00:20:39,601
- You!
- Yoo!

231
00:20:47,567 --> 00:20:49,333
<i>♪ Happy birthday to... ♪</i>

232
00:20:49,334 --> 00:20:52,634
- You!
- Yoo!

233
00:20:53,367 --> 00:20:56,167
What on earth are you all singing?

234
00:20:57,133 --> 00:20:58,434
Indraraja.

235
00:21:03,767 --> 00:21:05,634
There's no need to stand on ceremony.

236
00:21:09,133 --> 00:21:12,200
I'm here to give you my blessings
as your elder brother.

237
00:21:14,567 --> 00:21:15,667
Have a seat.

238
00:21:35,367 --> 00:21:36,467
Hey.

239
00:21:55,801 --> 00:21:57,200
Is that...

240
00:21:57,868 --> 00:22:02,566
the jade chest the Chin Haw merchant
gave Father?

241
00:22:02,567 --> 00:22:03,734
It is.

242
00:22:05,234 --> 00:22:06,834
It's yours now.

243
00:22:07,767 --> 00:22:09,067
Take it.

244
00:22:10,834 --> 00:22:11,901
I...

245
00:22:14,234 --> 00:22:17,133
- I can't accept it.
- Why not?

246
00:22:17,734 --> 00:22:19,501
Because I want you to have it!

247
00:22:26,133 --> 00:22:28,100
What a drunken fool.

248
00:22:30,801 --> 00:22:32,867
But I don't want it.

249
00:22:32,868 --> 00:22:35,166
It belongs to Father.

250
00:22:35,167 --> 00:22:36,433
You should keep it.

251
00:22:36,434 --> 00:22:39,032
How dare you disobey me, Kong Tai?

252
00:22:39,033 --> 00:22:41,367
I'm sure Kong Tai didn't mean to offend you.

253
00:22:47,234 --> 00:22:50,834
Perhaps he thinks your gift
is simply too precious to accept.

254
00:22:53,133 --> 00:22:54,600
You...

255
00:22:54,601 --> 00:22:59,834
Once I'm on the throne,
everything in this palace will be mine.

256
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:02,601
I can give whatever I want to whoever I please.

257
00:23:04,601 --> 00:23:06,334
Isn't that right?

258
00:23:31,067 --> 00:23:33,132
The Crown Prince...

259
00:23:33,133 --> 00:23:36,234
is simply trying to show
his generosity toward Kong Tai.

260
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:41,067
He may have been a little forceful
in making his offer,

261
00:23:41,734 --> 00:23:43,667
but I'm sure you understand.

262
00:23:46,968 --> 00:23:52,434
Indraraja has brought this jade chest,
a treasured possession of Father.

263
00:23:53,567 --> 00:23:55,467
Since he brought it to give you his blessing.

264
00:23:56,033 --> 00:24:01,400
Let's accept it
as a blessing from Father himself.

265
00:24:03,667 --> 00:24:06,033
As for a personal gift from Indraraja himself,

266
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:09,267
he'll arrange something else for you later.

267
00:24:10,033 --> 00:24:11,534
Would that satisfy you?

268
00:24:20,868 --> 00:24:22,200
Very well.

269
00:24:28,434 --> 00:24:30,233
I'll take my leave, then.

270
00:24:30,234 --> 00:24:33,067
Allow me to escort you back to your residence.

271
00:25:31,834 --> 00:25:34,634
Bottoms up!

272
00:25:42,067 --> 00:25:44,933
Hey! You're the birthday boy!

273
00:25:44,934 --> 00:25:47,399
You can't be the first one to pass out!

274
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:50,601
I can't keep up with you two!

275
00:25:54,234 --> 00:25:56,267
I have to concede defeat to you too, junior.

276
00:25:57,434 --> 00:26:00,933
You're quite the drinker.

277
00:26:00,934 --> 00:26:03,800
Then let's have another round. Come on.

278
00:26:03,801 --> 00:26:05,666
Lady Fongnuan.

279
00:26:05,667 --> 00:26:07,234
Senior.

280
00:26:08,133 --> 00:26:10,333
Lha.

281
00:26:10,334 --> 00:26:12,000
No, my lady.

282
00:26:13,133 --> 00:26:15,366
You really don't know a good thing
when you see it.

283
00:26:15,367 --> 00:26:17,234
Prince Kong Tai, keep going.

284
00:26:18,968 --> 00:26:20,399
Cheers!

285
00:26:20,400 --> 00:26:22,067
- Shia!
- Shia!

286
00:26:28,033 --> 00:26:30,333
Let's return to your residence, my lady.

287
00:26:30,334 --> 00:26:31,967
We can't leave yet, Lha.

288
00:26:31,968 --> 00:26:35,766
There's still plenty of liquor left.

289
00:26:35,767 --> 00:26:39,867
And this is homemade sato.

290
00:26:39,868 --> 00:26:43,067
I've never had sato this good.

291
00:26:43,667 --> 00:26:46,566
It'd be a shame to leave it unfinished.

292
00:26:46,567 --> 00:26:50,667
But Princess Maneethip
and Prince Saen Thep left ages ago.

293
00:26:51,834 --> 00:26:54,266
We shouldn't keep them waiting or worrying.

294
00:26:54,267 --> 00:26:56,666
Come on, Lha.

295
00:26:56,667 --> 00:26:59,833
Why do you have to bring up
those revered names?

296
00:26:59,834 --> 00:27:01,600
Fine. I'll stop drinking.

297
00:27:01,601 --> 00:27:03,266
I'm leaving now.

298
00:27:03,267 --> 00:27:07,233
Very well. I'll return to my residence.

299
00:27:07,234 --> 00:27:09,366
Enjoy yourselves, Your Highnesses.

300
00:27:09,367 --> 00:27:12,834
But next time, we're going to...

301
00:27:13,534 --> 00:27:15,901
drink till sunrise!

302
00:27:16,567 --> 00:27:19,400
Good night, Your Highness.
Good night. Good night.

303
00:27:20,334 --> 00:27:21,868
Good heavens, Lady Fongnuan!

304
00:27:23,934 --> 00:27:25,766
Good night! Good night!

305
00:27:25,767 --> 00:27:27,233
- Drink till sunrise.
- Lady Fongnuan.

306
00:27:27,234 --> 00:27:29,800
You're speaking that strange language again.

307
00:27:29,801 --> 00:27:31,266
Drink till sunrise?

308
00:27:31,267 --> 00:27:33,567
- Gud nai?
- What does that mean?

309
00:27:34,467 --> 00:27:35,868
Junior!

310
00:27:39,934 --> 00:27:43,267
We can... ask her again tomorrow.

311
00:27:49,334 --> 00:27:50,501
Here.

312
00:27:52,434 --> 00:27:54,666
- Shia!
- Shia!

313
00:27:54,667 --> 00:27:56,000
Shia.

314
00:28:00,334 --> 00:28:02,032
Good heavens!

315
00:28:02,033 --> 00:28:04,032
What's wrong, Kong Tai?

316
00:28:04,033 --> 00:28:08,467
The seer warned me
not to leave my residence after dark.

317
00:28:10,868 --> 00:28:12,601
And it's already late.

318
00:28:13,467 --> 00:28:14,767
I must go.

319
00:28:18,567 --> 00:28:20,067
Kong Tai.

320
00:28:34,801 --> 00:28:36,067
Shia!

321
00:28:42,968 --> 00:28:44,133
Shia.

322
00:29:03,567 --> 00:29:10,366
<i>♪ Happi birdday to yoo! ♪</i>

323
00:29:10,367 --> 00:29:12,466
<i>♪ Yoo! ♪</i>

324
00:29:12,467 --> 00:29:16,667
<i>♪ Birdday... yoo! ♪</i>

325
00:29:21,200 --> 00:29:22,600
Move!

326
00:29:22,601 --> 00:29:24,399
Get out of the way!

327
00:29:24,400 --> 00:29:25,834
Move!

328
00:29:26,968 --> 00:29:28,200
Move!

329
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:37,433
A woman.

330
00:29:37,434 --> 00:29:38,901
Pretty.

331
00:29:40,801 --> 00:29:42,234
Hey!

332
00:29:45,868 --> 00:29:47,501
No!

333
00:29:54,534 --> 00:29:56,267
Do you have a death wish?

334
00:29:59,834 --> 00:30:01,666
I was just singing.

335
00:30:01,667 --> 00:30:05,199
If you don't want to get hurt,
keep your shrill voice down.

336
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:06,801
You startled my horse.

337
00:30:11,734 --> 00:30:15,433
So, what's your name?

338
00:30:15,434 --> 00:30:18,266
I could sing for you instead.

339
00:30:18,267 --> 00:30:19,366
Just look at you.

340
00:30:19,367 --> 00:30:21,767
I doubt you could even find
your way back to your residence.

341
00:30:22,567 --> 00:30:24,601
Hey! Wait!

342
00:30:44,968 --> 00:30:49,868
<i>♪ Happi birdday to yoo! ♪</i>

343
00:31:06,567 --> 00:31:08,133
You should leave now.

344
00:31:23,734 --> 00:31:27,000
I've only just woken up,
and you're already trying to get rid of me.

345
00:31:37,767 --> 00:31:39,800
What's wrong?

346
00:31:39,801 --> 00:31:42,133
Why the long face?

347
00:31:49,300 --> 00:31:51,500
Your clothes...

348
00:31:51,501 --> 00:31:54,901
were made with exquisite skill
by master weavers.

349
00:31:57,400 --> 00:32:01,366
Your ornament is made of pure silver
and bears the royal emblem of the steed.

350
00:32:01,367 --> 00:32:05,233
It identifies you as
one of the King's six sons.

351
00:32:05,234 --> 00:32:07,333
A commoner like you

352
00:32:07,334 --> 00:32:11,467
could never have obtained such an ornament,
let alone stolen it.

353
00:32:12,634 --> 00:32:15,434
- You've been lying all this time.
- I never lied to you.

354
00:32:18,934 --> 00:32:20,968
I merely kept the truth from you.

355
00:32:24,767 --> 00:32:27,067
I had to hide who I was,

356
00:32:28,534 --> 00:32:30,801
but my love for you...

357
00:32:32,267 --> 00:32:33,801
is real.

358
00:32:35,033 --> 00:32:36,968
Every bit of it.

359
00:32:40,100 --> 00:32:42,534
You have two choices.

360
00:32:43,200 --> 00:32:46,967
First, never come here again.

361
00:32:46,968 --> 00:32:50,166
Second, you may keep coming here,

362
00:32:50,167 --> 00:32:51,733
but you must never see me again.

363
00:32:51,734 --> 00:32:53,267
I choose neither.

364
00:32:53,868 --> 00:32:58,132
I told you I wanted nothing to do
with people of high station.

365
00:32:58,133 --> 00:33:00,600
I dislike life in Wiang Kaew.

366
00:33:00,601 --> 00:33:02,967
If you ever try to buy my freedom,

367
00:33:02,968 --> 00:33:04,901
you'll never see me again.

368
00:33:10,901 --> 00:33:13,501
You cast me aside without a second thought.

369
00:33:15,234 --> 00:33:17,299
Do you not love me at all?

370
00:33:17,300 --> 00:33:19,300
All this time, I never knew.

371
00:33:19,968 --> 00:33:22,266
But now I do.

372
00:33:22,267 --> 00:33:24,667
I cannot accept it.

373
00:33:28,300 --> 00:33:31,567
Your world terrifies me.
I want no part of it.

374
00:33:36,434 --> 00:33:38,567
I want to live.

375
00:33:39,534 --> 00:33:41,501
Please, leave me be.

376
00:33:42,334 --> 00:33:43,934
We must never meet again.

377
00:34:42,234 --> 00:34:44,167
What happened here?

378
00:35:00,167 --> 00:35:02,100
Who did this?

379
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:11,334
Who did this?

380
00:35:15,133 --> 00:35:17,333
I did.

381
00:35:17,334 --> 00:35:20,299
I know you made these hawk's-eye amulets,

382
00:35:20,300 --> 00:35:22,633
but who destroyed them?

383
00:35:22,634 --> 00:35:24,366
Exactly.

384
00:35:24,367 --> 00:35:28,633
I'd like to know who could be so cruel, too.

385
00:35:28,634 --> 00:35:32,233
I spent days and nights making them.

386
00:35:32,234 --> 00:35:36,666
Lha even brought over a huge bundle of bamboo.
Then we carved them until our hands were raw.

387
00:35:36,667 --> 00:35:38,400
And now they're all ruined.

388
00:35:41,801 --> 00:35:44,366
Are you really so upset?

389
00:35:44,367 --> 00:35:46,067
Of course I am.

390
00:35:47,067 --> 00:35:49,032
They were meant to...

391
00:35:49,033 --> 00:35:53,166
bring blessings, ward off evil spirits,

392
00:35:53,167 --> 00:35:56,100
and protect Prince Kong Tai
from further misfortune.

393
00:35:57,868 --> 00:35:59,701
But look at them.

394
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:04,067
They're all ruined.
They can't protect anyone now.

395
00:36:06,667 --> 00:36:09,366
You seem to care a great deal about Kong Tai.

396
00:36:09,367 --> 00:36:13,166
You made him gifts, sang for him,

397
00:36:13,167 --> 00:36:15,434
and now you're even
collecting his gifts for him.

398
00:36:18,667 --> 00:36:20,667
You came here to retrieve something, too.

399
00:36:25,334 --> 00:36:27,600
If Prince Indraraja finds out,

400
00:36:27,601 --> 00:36:29,766
will there be another scene?

401
00:36:29,767 --> 00:36:33,267
As long as you keep quiet,
no one will find out.

402
00:36:34,033 --> 00:36:36,033
I'll take care of the rest.

403
00:36:39,100 --> 00:36:40,667
Prince Mueang Fah.

404
00:36:43,734 --> 00:36:46,133
You may seem rather stern,

405
00:36:46,701 --> 00:36:49,934
but you do care about your siblings.

406
00:37:02,234 --> 00:37:05,701
Yes, Your Highness. I'll say no more.

407
00:37:29,634 --> 00:37:31,934
Lha!

408
00:37:35,234 --> 00:37:39,067
Indraraja must have promised
to take him back to Ullavee.

409
00:37:39,767 --> 00:37:41,801
That's why he's taken Indraraja's side.

410
00:37:42,367 --> 00:37:47,266
Then why not ask Father
to lift the order of exile,

411
00:37:47,267 --> 00:37:50,100
and let Mueang Fah stay here with us?

412
00:37:50,801 --> 00:37:55,367
Then he would have no reason
to side with Indraraja.

413
00:37:58,267 --> 00:37:59,367
No.

414
00:38:01,300 --> 00:38:03,766
I don't want him anywhere near me.

415
00:38:03,767 --> 00:38:08,934
Ever since your brother arrived in Ullavee,
your father hasn't once asked to see me.

416
00:38:11,100 --> 00:38:12,800
He's a bringer of misfortune.

417
00:38:12,801 --> 00:38:17,166
Mother.
I doubt he has anything to do with that.

418
00:38:17,167 --> 00:38:20,800
Don't talk back to me.
Go earn some glory on the battlefield.

419
00:38:20,801 --> 00:38:23,733
The realm is at peace.

420
00:38:23,734 --> 00:38:25,667
Who am I supposed to fight?

421
00:38:27,200 --> 00:38:28,933
Then hurry up and marry.

422
00:38:28,934 --> 00:38:31,133
Find a consort of higher standing
than Saen Thep's.

423
00:38:34,400 --> 00:38:36,400
What does that have to do with anything?

424
00:38:38,267 --> 00:38:41,066
Through Saen Thep's marriage to Maneethip,

425
00:38:41,067 --> 00:38:44,000
your father has secured
a great deal of salt from Wang Nam Lin.

426
00:38:45,133 --> 00:38:47,133
Salt is scarce.

427
00:38:47,901 --> 00:38:52,166
Wang Nam Lin is a small city
with barely any troops.

428
00:38:52,167 --> 00:38:54,901
Its wealth comes entirely from its salt fields.

429
00:38:59,033 --> 00:39:01,666
You must find a consort

430
00:39:01,667 --> 00:39:03,968
who brings more than Saen Thep's does.

431
00:39:56,834 --> 00:39:59,800
Lady Fongnuan, don't you remember?

432
00:39:59,801 --> 00:40:02,533
Lha, just tell me.

433
00:40:02,534 --> 00:40:07,033
Then we can make her happy.

434
00:40:12,234 --> 00:40:14,800
Before she met Prince Saen Thep,

435
00:40:14,801 --> 00:40:17,734
Princess Maneethip was already in love
with someone else.

436
00:40:21,934 --> 00:40:24,000
General In Saeng.

437
00:40:27,701 --> 00:40:30,600
They had grown up together.

438
00:40:30,601 --> 00:40:34,533
General In Saeng was a loyal man.

439
00:40:34,534 --> 00:40:38,868
He had always protected
and looked after Princess Maneethip.

440
00:40:39,667 --> 00:40:43,467
He was also the one who taught her to ride.

441
00:40:48,200 --> 00:40:53,033
Over time, their closeness grew into love.

442
00:40:56,734 --> 00:41:00,900
But before they could confess their feelings,

443
00:41:00,901 --> 00:41:04,868
Prince Saen Thep met Princess Maneethip.

444
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:33,333
His Highness asked King Chai Saen Lue

445
00:41:33,334 --> 00:41:36,868
to send a royal proposal
for Princess Maneethip's hand in marriage.

446
00:41:38,634 --> 00:41:40,967
Your uncle agreed to the match.

447
00:41:40,968 --> 00:41:46,234
He approved Princess Maneethip's
marriage to Prince Saen Thep.

448
00:41:47,100 --> 00:41:51,701
And he sent General In Saeng
to serve at the city border.

449
00:42:14,033 --> 00:42:16,834
And we were sent here.

450
00:42:17,734 --> 00:42:19,900
From that day on,

451
00:42:19,901 --> 00:42:24,666
Princess Maneethip and General In Saeng

452
00:42:24,667 --> 00:42:26,801
never saw each other again.

453
00:42:30,033 --> 00:42:35,534
Wang Nam Lin is a small city
with no army to speak of.

454
00:42:36,467 --> 00:42:40,934
We must depend on Ullavee,
a far greater kingdom.

455
00:42:43,968 --> 00:42:48,367
Prince Saen Thep is third in line
to the throne.

456
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:56,433
Your uncle needs Ullavee's military strength

457
00:42:56,434 --> 00:43:00,434
to keep the bandits and rebels at bay.

458
00:43:09,367 --> 00:43:15,400
It was a marriage of convenience,

459
00:43:16,467 --> 00:43:18,367
not love.

460
00:43:22,000 --> 00:43:24,767
Even after hundreds of years,

461
00:43:26,567 --> 00:43:28,267
such arrangements...

462
00:43:29,367 --> 00:43:31,067
still exist.

463
00:43:35,000 --> 00:43:36,901
Is it possible...

464
00:43:38,400 --> 00:43:41,200
to marry someone for love,

465
00:43:44,334 --> 00:43:46,934
out of genuine affection,

466
00:43:48,033 --> 00:43:51,166
with nothing to gain from it?

467
00:43:51,167 --> 00:43:53,234
That would be difficult, my lady.

468
00:43:54,100 --> 00:43:57,366
Princes and princesses

469
00:43:57,367 --> 00:44:00,601
must always marry out of duty.

470
00:44:04,901 --> 00:44:09,534
But Prince Saen Thep
treats Princess Maneethip very well.

471
00:44:10,767 --> 00:44:13,367
He does everything he can to pamper her.

472
00:44:15,200 --> 00:44:19,200
Yet Princess Maneethip
still refuses to open her heart to him.

473
00:44:23,601 --> 00:44:26,100
My heart aches for them both.

474
00:44:29,834 --> 00:44:34,801
I hope she and Prince Saen Thep...

475
00:44:38,701 --> 00:44:40,667
can get through this.

476
00:44:44,200 --> 00:44:45,801
At least...

477
00:44:46,534 --> 00:44:49,434
their wedding night...

478
00:44:53,434 --> 00:44:56,701
should be a happy occasion for them both.

479
00:45:42,634 --> 00:45:45,467
- I bow before you, Royal Consort Sukantha.
- I bow before you, Royal Consort Sukantha.

480
00:45:47,200 --> 00:45:50,133
- I bow before you, Royal Consort Chiang La-or.
- I bow before you, Royal Consort Chiang La-or.

481
00:45:53,100 --> 00:45:58,066
We are deeply honored
by your presence, Royal Consort Sukantha.

482
00:45:58,067 --> 00:46:02,567
As the inner court's representative,
it is my duty to attend.

483
00:46:08,400 --> 00:46:10,434
What a modest ceremony.

484
00:46:11,067 --> 00:46:15,734
Quite fitting for a consort from a small city
like Wang Nam Lin.

485
00:47:01,567 --> 00:47:05,100
What does the full bedding ceremony involve?

486
00:47:06,200 --> 00:47:10,199
After the Soul-Blessing Ceremony,
which wards off misfortune

487
00:47:10,200 --> 00:47:13,666
and blesses the bride and groom
with a lifetime of love.

488
00:47:13,667 --> 00:47:17,066
Their family members tie blessed cotton threads
around their wrists.

489
00:47:17,067 --> 00:47:19,434
And offer them their blessings.

490
00:47:20,033 --> 00:47:22,000
Then the couple is escorted
to the bridal chamber.

491
00:47:28,667 --> 00:47:30,132
There.

492
00:47:30,133 --> 00:47:32,133
The master of ceremonies is here.

493
00:47:36,701 --> 00:47:38,234
The fortune teller?

494
00:47:51,434 --> 00:47:52,968
What fortune teller?

495
00:47:54,934 --> 00:47:56,433
That uncle.

496
00:47:56,434 --> 00:47:57,868
Who is he, Your Highness?

497
00:47:58,934 --> 00:48:00,500
Seer Phrommaya.

498
00:48:00,501 --> 00:48:05,500
Royal Consort Chiang La-or invited him
to conduct the blessing ceremony.

499
00:48:05,501 --> 00:48:06,734
A seer?

500
00:48:07,767 --> 00:48:09,434
A royal seer?

501
00:48:10,801 --> 00:48:12,667
What in the world?

502
00:48:24,667 --> 00:48:26,399
Goodness!

503
00:48:26,400 --> 00:48:27,833
What took you so long?

504
00:48:27,834 --> 00:48:30,200
I thought you'd show up at the end
to help clean up.

505
00:48:31,934 --> 00:48:34,867
I went to fetch Fah Haam first.

506
00:48:34,868 --> 00:48:37,099
I had to drag him out of bed.

507
00:48:37,100 --> 00:48:38,701
Now I'm starving.

508
00:48:39,801 --> 00:48:41,968
Is food all you ever think about?

509
00:48:45,133 --> 00:48:48,266
What happened to you?

510
00:48:48,267 --> 00:48:52,533
Goodness!
Did you fall into a wine barrel, Your Highness?

511
00:48:52,534 --> 00:48:55,733
Just look at you.
You look like a man with a broken heart.

512
00:48:55,734 --> 00:48:58,566
Do they have any sato?
Can I have a drink now?

513
00:48:58,567 --> 00:49:02,266
Please? Will you stop asking for a drink?

514
00:49:02,267 --> 00:49:05,133
Have some mercy.
I have to observe the Five Precepts.

515
00:49:22,634 --> 00:49:24,167
Mueang Fah.

516
00:49:32,067 --> 00:49:33,334
Bew!

517
00:49:41,934 --> 00:49:43,100
<i>Babe.</i>

518
00:49:46,234 --> 00:49:48,534
<i>Here, here. Hey!</i>

519
00:49:51,400 --> 00:49:55,300
<i>- That hurts.
- I'm sorry.</i>

520
00:50:07,133 --> 00:50:08,400
Bew?

521
00:50:21,634 --> 00:50:27,399
After Indraraja, Mueang Fah,
and Prince Pha Wiang arrived.

522
00:50:27,400 --> 00:50:29,733
Why do you look like you've seen a ghost?

523
00:50:29,734 --> 00:50:31,999
A ghost would've been better.

524
00:50:32,000 --> 00:50:34,400
I never want to see him again in this lifetime.

525
00:50:35,968 --> 00:50:38,132
Wait, what's the name of the man

526
00:50:38,133 --> 00:50:42,800
who just arrived
with Prince Indraraja and Prince Mueang Fah?

527
00:50:42,801 --> 00:50:44,467
Prince Pha Wiang.

528
00:50:47,467 --> 00:50:49,833
The Crown Prince of Merng Mang.

529
00:50:49,834 --> 00:50:52,200
He's Indraraja's cousin.

530
00:50:53,634 --> 00:50:57,600
Prince Pha Wiang's father was
the elder brother of Indraraja's mother,

531
00:50:57,601 --> 00:51:00,033
the late Queen Chao Oun.

532
00:51:00,834 --> 00:51:02,000
Junior.

533
00:51:03,067 --> 00:51:04,501
Do you know him?

534
00:51:11,267 --> 00:51:13,133
No, Your Highness.

535
00:51:14,968 --> 00:51:17,132
I don't. That's why I asked.

536
00:51:17,133 --> 00:51:22,200
I don't want to put my foot in my mouth
and end up losing my head.

537
00:51:23,801 --> 00:51:25,600
Well, then...

538
00:51:25,601 --> 00:51:27,867
I'll take my leave.

539
00:51:27,868 --> 00:51:30,501
I'd rather go see Maneethip.

540
00:51:46,234 --> 00:51:47,734
Fah Haam.

541
00:51:50,400 --> 00:51:52,167
Don't handle me so roughly,

542
00:51:52,767 --> 00:51:54,133
or I might throw up.

543
00:51:55,067 --> 00:51:58,467
I was only going to ask you to move over.
I need to sit down.

544
00:52:09,667 --> 00:52:11,601
This might make you feel better.

545
00:52:21,334 --> 00:52:23,701
That's Prince Pha Wiang, Boon.

546
00:52:24,901 --> 00:52:26,534
He's not Bew.

547
00:52:30,567 --> 00:52:32,333
That woman.

548
00:52:32,334 --> 00:52:34,266
Who is she?

549
00:52:34,267 --> 00:52:37,266
Lady Fongnuan,
a younger cousin of Princess Maneethip,

550
00:52:37,267 --> 00:52:39,533
Prince Saen Thep's consort.

551
00:52:39,534 --> 00:52:41,366
I see.

552
00:52:41,367 --> 00:52:42,968
So she's no stranger to the court.

553
00:52:44,834 --> 00:52:47,099
But she seems a little unhinged.

554
00:52:47,100 --> 00:52:48,667
Quite mad.

555
00:53:07,133 --> 00:53:09,067
Your bride has arrived.

556
00:53:46,200 --> 00:53:47,901
I know you're exhausted,

557
00:53:49,000 --> 00:53:52,167
but remember to keep smiling
throughout today's ceremony.

558
00:54:39,934 --> 00:54:41,934
Please take good care
of my cousin, Your Highness.

559
00:55:13,934 --> 00:55:17,834
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.

560
00:55:18,534 --> 00:55:20,400
King Chai Saen Lue.

561
00:56:20,467 --> 00:56:22,333
These blessed cotton threads...

562
00:56:22,334 --> 00:56:26,566
will bind your wrists for this night alone,

563
00:56:26,567 --> 00:56:30,999
but may love bind...

564
00:56:31,000 --> 00:56:33,968
your hearts for all eternity.

565
00:56:34,901 --> 00:56:38,000
May you love and cherish each other,

566
00:56:38,734 --> 00:56:41,968
and be blessed with many children
and grandchildren.

567
00:57:39,467 --> 00:57:45,934
<i>According to records from neighboring cities,
Ullavee's last king was a cruel man.</i>

568
00:57:46,501 --> 00:57:50,334
<i>He killed his own siblings to seize the throne.</i>

569
00:57:54,634 --> 00:57:58,566
<i>Most of the princes had different mothers,</i>

570
00:57:58,567 --> 00:58:01,433
<i>yet they'd been close since childhood.</i>

571
00:58:01,434 --> 00:58:04,633
<i>Alas, no matter how much
they loved one another,</i>

572
00:58:04,634 --> 00:58:09,701
<i>when the time came to fight for power,
the struggle was brutal.</i>

573
00:58:56,467 --> 00:58:59,067
Today is the happiest day of my life.

574
00:58:59,968 --> 00:59:02,434
I'm so glad you're my consort.

575
00:59:05,801 --> 00:59:10,868
I promise to love and care for you.

576
00:59:13,367 --> 00:59:15,734
I'll never cause you sorrow.

577
00:59:43,667 --> 00:59:45,701
So this is your answer.

578
00:59:52,334 --> 00:59:53,968
All this time,

579
00:59:56,167 --> 00:59:58,467
you never wished to marry me,

580
01:00:02,434 --> 01:00:05,200
nor did you ever love me, did you?

581
01:00:15,467 --> 01:00:17,367
My feelings...

582
01:00:19,200 --> 01:00:20,801
are of no consequence.

583
01:00:28,434 --> 01:00:31,234
Duty must come before the heart, Your Highness.

584
01:01:10,601 --> 01:01:12,701
My cousin is married now.

585
01:01:13,367 --> 01:01:15,601
It's just the two of us left.

586
01:01:16,667 --> 01:01:18,666
It feels a little lonely, doesn't it?

587
01:01:18,667 --> 01:01:20,000
Yes, my lady.

588
01:01:34,267 --> 01:01:35,567
Lha.

589
01:01:38,534 --> 01:01:40,367
On the wedding night,

590
01:01:41,968 --> 01:01:44,501
isn't it considered bad luck...

591
01:01:45,934 --> 01:01:47,701
to leave the bridal chamber?

592
01:01:50,033 --> 01:01:51,767
It is, my lady.

593
01:01:52,968 --> 01:01:55,400
Once inside the bridal chamber,

594
01:01:56,767 --> 01:01:59,999
the bride and groom must remain there
together throughout the night.

595
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:03,299
They must not leave the room until morning,

596
01:02:03,300 --> 01:02:05,100
or else...

597
01:02:11,234 --> 01:02:13,801
their marriage is believed to be short-lived.

598
01:02:47,234 --> 01:02:49,033
Women do not drink.

599
01:02:49,734 --> 01:02:51,234
It is improper.

600
01:02:51,868 --> 01:02:54,933
I'm not drinking as a woman.

601
01:02:54,934 --> 01:02:57,733
I'm drinking as someone willing to listen.

602
01:02:57,734 --> 01:03:00,600
I won't say a word.

603
01:03:00,601 --> 01:03:03,800
Whatever is on your mind, you can tell me.

604
01:03:03,801 --> 01:03:05,567
I'll listen.

605
01:03:06,267 --> 01:03:08,200
I have nothing to say.

606
01:03:08,868 --> 01:03:13,033
Then... we can drink in silence.

607
01:03:41,934 --> 01:03:43,734
Your older cousin...

608
01:03:46,267 --> 01:03:48,734
cried on her wedding night.

609
01:03:53,000 --> 01:03:54,968
I don't know why.

610
01:03:58,434 --> 01:04:00,667
I only know that she's unhappy.

611
01:04:05,067 --> 01:04:07,934
How can our marriage ever work...

612
01:04:10,467 --> 01:04:12,601
when the man who is supposed
to be her life partner...

613
01:04:13,601 --> 01:04:15,968
can't make her happy?

614
01:04:19,734 --> 01:04:21,767
I don't deserve her.

615
01:04:23,801 --> 01:04:26,533
My cousin and you...

616
01:04:26,534 --> 01:04:28,868
are well suited for each other.

617
01:04:31,000 --> 01:04:33,200
But perhaps you just need time.

618
01:04:34,133 --> 01:04:37,701
Once Maneethip gets to know you better,

619
01:04:38,667 --> 01:04:41,267
I'm sure she'll be happy.

620
01:04:43,067 --> 01:04:44,634
You know that.

621
01:04:49,534 --> 01:04:52,000
How can your cousin not see that?

622
01:05:04,767 --> 01:05:06,734
Your words...

623
01:05:07,934 --> 01:05:09,801
bring me comfort.

624
01:05:10,567 --> 01:05:12,701
At least I have you,

625
01:05:13,868 --> 01:05:17,099
who sees something good in me.

626
01:05:17,100 --> 01:05:18,801
Of course I do.

627
01:05:19,701 --> 01:05:23,299
You're calm and gentle.

628
01:05:23,300 --> 01:05:25,900
You can be a little strict at times,

629
01:05:25,901 --> 01:05:27,868
but that's only because you care.

630
01:05:30,601 --> 01:05:34,968
Maneethip is the luckiest woman...
to have you as her life partner.

631
01:05:37,100 --> 01:05:42,367
Then I'm lucky...
to have spoken with you tonight, too.

632
01:05:44,367 --> 01:05:46,534
Any man who has you as his life partner...

633
01:05:48,767 --> 01:05:51,200
would be the luckiest man alive.

634
01:05:52,801 --> 01:05:54,934
More like the most unfortunate.

635
01:06:42,033 --> 01:06:43,766
<i>Which way is Wat Khao Nam Saeng?</i>
[Next Episode]

636
01:06:43,767 --> 01:06:47,366
<i>If you wish to find out,
get in the boat and help me pick lotuses.</i>

637
01:06:47,367 --> 01:06:49,200
<i>You'll bruise it if you hold it like that.</i>

638
01:06:52,634 --> 01:06:57,166
<i>I wish to know everything about Maneethip,
especially her past.</i>

639
01:06:57,167 --> 01:07:01,833
<i>If Your Majesty would grant me a favor,
I have a request to make.</i>

640
01:07:01,834 --> 01:07:02,668
<i>Speak.</i>

641
01:07:02,669 --> 01:07:07,466
<i>The King has issued a royal decree
appointing Lady Fongnuan</i>

642
01:07:07,467 --> 01:07:11,166
<i>as an outer court lady-in-waiting at the
in Wiang Kaew,</i>

643
01:07:11,167 --> 01:07:12,800
<i>effective immediately.</i>

644
01:07:12,801 --> 01:07:16,032
<i>She may have been meant
to serve at the inner court.</i>

645
01:07:16,033 --> 01:07:18,533
<i>Fongnuan was appointed
an outer court lady-in-waiting,</i>

646
01:07:18,534 --> 01:07:20,333
<i>not the inner court.</i>

647
01:07:20,334 --> 01:07:21,633
<i>Look into this matter.</i>

648
01:07:21,634 --> 01:07:23,666
<i>It is important to both of us.</i>

649
01:07:23,667 --> 01:07:25,166
<i>I wish to be prepared.</i>

650
01:07:25,167 --> 01:07:27,132
<i>You should accept this royal decree.</i>

651
01:07:27,133 --> 01:07:29,667
<i>Accept the royal decree at once, Fongnuan.</i>
